    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d473-a2">

                <pb facs="0832" n="736" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg736"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    121.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mejia to Mr.
                            Lafragua.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Finance</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1874-03-06"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 6,
                    1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Citizen Minister of Foreign
                        Affairs</hi>:</p>
                <p>Under date of yesterday the citizen treasurer-general of the nation says to me
                    the following:</p>
                <p>“In compliance with the supreme order No. 616, of yesterday, to the effect that I
                    send you, as quickly as possible, a statement of Mexican bonds issued in the New
                    York market, I have the honor to report as follows: 1. That of the $2,950,000 of
                    bonds issued in San Carlos de Tamaulipas on the 4th of July, 1865, by the
                    Citizen-General J. M. J. Carbajal, there remain unfunded $1,438,050, in 6,368
                    bonds, as follows:</p>
                <table cols="3" rows="4">
                    <row role="label">
                        <cell role="num">695</cell>
                        <cell>bonds, letter L, of $50 each</cell>
                        <cell role="num">$34,750</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell role="num">3,583</cell>
                        <cell>bonds, letter C, of $100 each</cell>
                        <cell role="num">358,300</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell rendition="#border-bottom" role="num">2,090</cell>
                        <cell>bonds, letter D, of $500 each</cell>
                        <cell rendition="#border-bottom" role="num">1,045,000</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell role="num">6,368</cell>
                        <cell>bond, of the value of</cell>
                        <cell role="num">1,438,050</cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <p>“2. That of the $10,000,000 in bonds, issued by the Citizen-General Gaspar
                    Sanchez Ochoa, in San Francisco, Cal., on the 1st of July, 1865, there remain
                    unfunded $500,000, and these, according to the data existing in this treasury,
                    are detained in the custody of Eugene Kelly &amp; Co., of New York, by order of
                    supreme court of that State. The numeration of the bonds corresponding to said
                    $500,000 is not specified, because no information is obtainable as to the
                    numeration of those which were lost at sea in May, 1868, on board the steamer
                    Nevada, which represented a value of $3,750,000, nor of the actual bonds
                    detained in the hands of Kelly &amp; Co., as above mentioned.”</p>
                <p>And I have the honor to transcribe the above to you, as the result of your
                    communication of the 2d instant.</p>
                <p>Independence and liberty.</p>
                <closer><signed>MEJIA.</signed></closer>
            </div>
